{"t": 1794125059.7015138, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fix/pagination-57", "files": [{"content": "def page(items: list, number: int, size: int) -> list:\n    start = (number - 1) * size\n    return items[start:start + size]\n", "path": "catalog/pager.py"}, {"content": "import pytest\n\nfrom catalog.pager import page\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    (\"items\", \"number\", \"size\", \"expected\"),\n    [\n        ([0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 1, 2, [0, 1]),\n        ([0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 2, 2, [2, 3]),\n        ([0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 3, 2, [4]),\n        ([0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 4, 2, []),\n        ([], 1, 2, []),\n    ],\n)\ndef test_page_uses_one_based_numbers(items, number, size, expected):\n    assert page(items, number, size) == expected\n", "path": "tests/test_pager.py"}], "message": "Fix one-based pagination offset (#57) and add regression tests", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794125063.0960677, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "Fixes #57.\n\nIssue #57 specifies 1-based page numbers. Compute the slice offset as (number - 1) * size so page 1 returns the first page.\n\nAdds regression coverage for the first and second pages, a partial last page, an out-of-range page, and empty input. No new behavior is specified for invalid page numbers or sizes.\n\nValidation: python -m pytest -q \u2014 5 passed locally.", "draft": false, "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix one-based pagination offset (#57)"}, "ok": true}
